---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title={`Accessibility Statement — ${site.name}`}
  description={`${site.name}'s commitment to an accessible website, and how to report a problem.`}
  locale="en"
  path="/accessibility/"
>
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: August 28, 2026</em></p>

    <p>
      We want this site to work for everyone, including people using a
      screen reader, keyboard-only navigation, or a browser's built-in
      zoom or high-contrast mode. This page says what we're doing about
      that and how to reach us if something isn't working.
    </p>

    <h2>What we're aiming for</h2>
    <p>
      We build this site to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines
      (WCAG) 2.1 at Level AA — things like readable color contrast, a
      logical heading structure, working keyboard navigation, a "skip to
      content" link, and alt text on every image. This is an ongoing
      effort, not a one-time checkbox — we review it periodically and fix
      what we find.
    </p>

    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <p>
      We're not aware of any at the moment. If you run into one, that's
      exactly what the contact below is for.
    </p>

    <h2>Report a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If any part of this site is hard to use with assistive technology,
      or you hit a barrier we haven't caught, email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with what page you
      were on and what happened. We'll look into it directly — this isn't
      a form-letter inbox.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
